H5_v3s_lobe_growth: v3s's D.P < 0 lobes -- the khronon velocity relative to the lobe, and the e-folds
mutate = False; kappa = 1/2 FITTED; footings never pooled; one thread, nice 15

A: the khronon velocity relative to a moving system's lobe (sympy)
  A1: EL_sigma + [d_t rho_tau + div(rho_tau v_tau)] = 0; EL_phi - [lap phi - K(rho_m + rho_tau)]/K = 0; D_t v_tau + grad(phi - Xi) = [0, 0] (rho_tau = div P - mu_K^2 Xi/K, v_tau = -grad sigma)
A1 PASS residuals 0, 0, [0, 0] all identically 0
  A2: x = x' + V t, sigma' = sigma + V.x' + V^2 t/2: Xi' - Xi = 0; v' - (v - V) = [0, 0]. The static branch (v_tau = 0) holds only in the khronon rest frame; in a frame moving at V the same fluid has v' = -V
A2 PASS Xi' - Xi = 0; v' - (v - V) = [0, 0] identically 0
  A3: steady linear response, system frame, host background (rhobar > 0, field n), stiffness gamma_L Theta:
      (i)  d rho_tau - d rho_m / [M(k) - 1 + Theta L*^2 k^2/2 - (k.V)^2/(K rhobar)] = 0
      (ii) V = 0, Theta = 1: d rho_tau / d rho_m - m/(1 - m + kappa^2 m/2) [D10 Route F kernel] = 0
      (iii) V -> inf: (k.V)^2 d rho_tau + K rhobar d rho_m = 0; d psi + K d rho_m/k^2 = 0; d v - k d psi/(k.V) = 0
      => static limit = the screened phantom (lobes from the anisotropic M); flow-through limit = the cold wake of the
         baryons' Newtonian potential, amplitude proportional to rhobar; crossover V_* = sqrt(K rhobar (M-1) + gamma_L rhobar k^2)/k
A3 PASS (i) 0, (ii) 0, (iii) 0, 0, 0 all identically 0
  A4: rho = rho0(X)/det(dx/dX) in Lagrangian continuity D_t rho + rho div v: residual 0 -> the sign of rho_tau is carried along v_tau (before caustics); rho_tau > 0 in, rho_tau > 0 out
A4 PASS residual 0 identically 0
  A5: Danby-Camm steady continuity max |div(rho v)| r/(rho_inf V) = 8.25e-15 (200 points, 2 parameter sets); energy |v|^2 = V^2 + 2GM/r to 7.5e-15; rho/rho_inf - 1 - (b-R)^2/[R(2b-R)] = 0
      numerical Lagrangian (attractive point mass, DOP853 rtol 1e-12, 25 points): max |rho_num/rho_DC - 1| = 1.01e-06, min rho_num/rho_inf = 1.000388
A5 PASS continuity 8.3e-15; identity 0; Lagrangian dev 1.0e-06, min 1.000388, n 25 <= 1e-9; 0; <= 1e-3 with min >= 1 at >= 20 points
      reported: NGC 2419 Plummer (GM/(V^2 a) = 6.30e-03 at V = 167 km/s), 84 points at r >= 9 a: rho/rho_inf in [1.00000000, 1.00440781], max |rho_Plummer/rho_DC,point - 1| = 2.8e-03

